35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The late-turn pool is hollow. Overtime covers final departures and overnight works. We cannot promise more hours without breaking the existing schedule.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"The stopwatch says mid-city is slow, but platforms clear fast. The real time loss is waiting for connections, not paying.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The ledger holds a ring-fenced grant, but operating subsidies are cut. Ticketing fees now exceed paving budgets. We are paying for the past, not the future.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The pilots succeeded. The accessibility work mostly held, though lane priorities failed. We must learn from these specific outcomes, not just repeat the enthusiasm.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,The minutes show the ferry and rail back offices never agreed on data terms. The shells hide voids that stop work for weeks.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, if ticketing fees eat the paving budget, we can't fund the physical upgrades. I need to know if the maintenance contract has spare capacity to cover the gap.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, spare capacity is a trap. The data proves connections are the bottleneck, not the machines. We must fix the waiting, not the ticketing.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, you’re ignoring the cash flow. If fees exceed paving, we can’t even maintain the lanes you want to fix.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, the cash flow is real, but the memory is sharper. The pilots proved the late-night model works. We must not let the ledger silence a proven success.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, the pilots worked because they avoided the shells. I am checking who else must sign off before we trust any date.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, the maintenance contract has spare capacity for lifts, but the roster books show the late-turn pool is empty. We cannot extend hours without breaking the existing schedule.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, spare capacity doesn't fix broken connections. The data shows waiting is the killer, not the machines. We must fix the flow, not the ticketing.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, spare capacity is a band-aid. If the ledger is bleeding, we can’t buy the overtime to keep the lights on, let alone extend them.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, the rosters are thin, yes. But the pilot proved the late-night model recovers its cost. We must not let fear of the present erase a proven success.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Asuka, the shells are the trap. Three jobs stopped for weeks on voids. I need to know who else must sign off before we trust any date.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, the pilot recovered costs, but it did not fix the empty rosters. We cannot extend hours if the people to run them are already exhausted.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, exhausted crews don't fix slow connections. The data proves waiting is the killer. We must fix the flow, not the ticketing.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, exhaustion is a symptom of the ledger. If the ring-fenced grant is locked, we can’t buy the overtime to keep the lights on, let alone extend them.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, exhaustion is real, but the pilot proved the model works. We must not let current fatigue erase a proven, cost-recovering success.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Asuka, the rosters are thin, but the shells are the real trap. I need to know who else must sign off before we trust any date.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
